Subject: Export package-qualified runtime executable paths

Applies to: rosdistro lyrical.2026-10-05.rcr.4, ament/ament_index.bzl.

Observed failure: ros2 pkg executables rclcpp_components returns no entries,
and ros2 run cannot find component_container in an extracted native runtime.
ament_index registers executables under bin/, while standard ROS CLI discovery
looks under lib/<package>/. The installed ament_package layout already performs
that package-qualified mapping.

Rationale and scope: add lib/<package>/<basename> aliases for the same declared
executable files. Retain bin/ aliases and existing runfiles propagation. Do not
infer ownership from an aggregate bin directory or change component sources.

Verification: //third_party/rosdistro:executable_index_test passes with
--config=runtime --config=no-agnocast. It verifies both aliases refer to the
same file and exercises standard package discovery, executable lookup and a
real subprocess. The consuming distribution has a separate extracted CLI gate.

Upstream: the selected published rule lacks these aliases, inspected
2026-11-23. No matching upstream association is recorded.
https://bazel.ros.org/modules/rosdistro/lyrical.2026-10-05.rcr.4/source.json

--- a/ament/ament_index.bzl
+++ b/ament/ament_index.bzl
@@ -208,0 +209 @@
+            symlinks["lib/" + package_name + "/" + file.basename] = file
